egree burns over 80  percent of his body the fire broke out  in the intensive care ward of the  hospital  which is located about 350 kilometers  north of the country's capital  romania's health minister says it likely  started as the result of a short circuit  the country has recorded more than 353  000 cases of kova 19 since the start of  the pandemic  still had the temporary tents pitched as  a lasting protection  for health care workers  you're watching global national  as cobit 19 cases surge across the  country  the safety of health care workers is a  critical concern  many hospitals are being stretched to  their limits and they need  all hands on deck now a made in canada  device could reduce the risk to those  working on the front lines while saving  lives  su lingo reports shortly after  covid19 cases hit edmonton emergency  room physician mark curiel was inserting  a tube in a patient's windpipe  when he realized how unprotected he was  my mask didn't fit because i didn't  shave that day  so i'm wearing my mask and i'm feeling  air leaking in the sides and the whole  time i'm thinking  what am i going to be bringing home to  my family he reached out to a friend  mechanical engineer chris tariff to  brainstorm a solution they came up  with this an aerosol containment tent  it uses suction and a hepa filter to  remove  any covid infected droplets from the air  really the concept is build a portable  negative pressure area over a patient's  head  and we built it aerosol generating  procedures such as intubation  bipap and ventilation can spray  particles up to 10 meters away  which can stay infectious for up to  three hours  dr curiel says the pandemic has changed  how they do things in hospitals  i have not used bypass since kobit  started and this is a technique that  would  get people better faster and instead of  sending them to the icu  we can send them to the regular medicine  floor this tent would allow  airway procedures to be done safely  anywhere  it